  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Python wheel. Offline installation follows author removal; unchanged callers replay after moving the installed tree on both CPython floors, giving four executions per selection. The full API checks per-site constructors, normalization, repeated record fields, active variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards, rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Primitive-base nominal Python acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete wheels from two authors. CPython 3.11.16 and 3.12.14 install the same wheel offline after author removal and replay after physical relocation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor. Original wheels, receipts, process records, environment closures and selected sources are retained; external toolchain binaries are not. Other hosts need their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
